 simplifying, and substituting in the given information, we have \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}25‖v{‖}^{2}+2‖v+w{‖}^{2} & =25‖v{‖}^{2}+2(‖v{‖}^{2}+‖w{‖}^{2}) \\\\  & =25‖v{‖}^{2}+2(‖v{‖}^{2}+{5}^{2}) \\\\  & =27‖v{‖}^{2}+50.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nCombining the two steps above, we get \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}158 & \\le 27‖v‖+50 \\\\ 108 & \\le 27‖v{‖}^{2} \\\\ 4 & \\le ‖v{‖}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, $4\\le ‖v{‖}^{2}$ implies that $2\\le ‖v‖.$ Notice that we disregard the negative solutions since the norm can't be negative.\n\nTherefore, the minimum possible value of $‖v‖$ is $2.$" 13194139535018 true] [17592186327118 1000 #edb/ref 17592186327119 13194139535018 true] [17592186327118 1000 #edb/ref 17592186327120 13194139535018 true] [17592186327118 1000 #edb/ref 17592186327121 13194139535018 true] [17592186327118 1000 #edb/ref 17592186327122 13194139535018 true] [17592186327118 1000 #edb/ref 17592186327123 13194139535018 true] [17592186327118 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535018 true] [17592186327118 1041 "selection" 13194139535018 true] [17592186327118 1104 #edb/ref 17592186327121 13194139535018 true] [17592186327118 1110 #uuid "b4e7400e-0173-5326-a9d8-237cca1079a7" 13194139535018 true] [17592186327119 1034 "\\sqrt{2}" 13194139535018 true] [17592186327119 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535018 true] [17592186327119 1111 #uuid "cf41f401-e0dd-5e32-bdaa-9fc27ac52864" 13194139535018 true] [17592186327120 1034 "\\sqrt{3}" 13194139535018 true] [17592186327120 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535018 true] [17592186327120 1111 #uuid "7c6ea1f7-4bda-57b0-8037-cf6086307d85" 13194139535018 true] [17592186327121 1034 "2" 13194139535018 true] [17592186327121 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535018 true] [17592186327121 1111 #uuid "3aa45136-9e3d-58c6-93eb-16148c84a764" 13194139535018 true] [17592186327122 1034 "1" 13194139535018 true] [17592186327122 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535018 true] [17592186327122 1111 #uuid "09cb2125-ab2e-50a7-b8fc-dd863601f